title: Klinefelter's Syndrome
---

# Klinefelter's Syndrome

- **Definition** - chromosomal disorder in male most associated with 47XXY karyotype
- **Pathophysiology** - progressive dysgenesis of semineferous tubules:
  - <u>Progressive fibrosis and hyalinsation of semineferous tubules</u> - subsequently results in infertility
  - <u>Leydig cell dysfunction</u> - results in male hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism with characteristic effects on growth and development
- **Clinical feature** - typically diagnosed in adolescence with gynaecomastia and failure to progress through puberty:
  - **Tall stature** - apparent in erly childhood with characteristic long legs exacerbated by androgen deficiency with lack of epiphyseal closure
  - **Gynaecomastia** - often attributed to male hypogonadism
  - **Other associated features:**
    - Learning difficulties and behavioural disorders
    - Increased risk of T2DM
    - Increased risk of breast cancer
    - Infertility
- **Ix and Dx** - hormone profiling demonstrates characteristic hypergonadotrophic hypogonadism, and Dx made on karyotype
- **Mx** - androgen replacement
